1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,000
National Radio and Television Administration

2
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Welcome to Sister Pang's Bathhouse

3
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,479
Dong Beihu, you...

4
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:37,320
Where is your alcohol dehydrogenase? Where is it?

5
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:38,479
Where is...

6
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,560
Shut up. Hurry.

7
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,880
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

8
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,320
So embarrassing.

9
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:49,120
Life is but a few short autumns.

10
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,920
Why are you here?

11
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,160
In the east, my...

12
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:04,720
Get in.

13
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:33,240
What a coincidence.

14
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:39,040
Super coincidental. I just happened to pass by.

15
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,560
What do you mean, pass by?

16
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,680
Your place isn't on the way.

17
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,560
Did you move?

18
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:48,610
I was afraid you'd get too drunk to go home.

19
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,940
I can handle my liquor.

20
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:53,560
I'm telling you,

21
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,760
if you judge like this,

22
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,420
I definitely won't accept it.

23
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,560
Okay, let's go.

24
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,480
I haven't finished yet. Put the cup down.

25
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:00,000
Put the cup down.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,760
Can't we just have a nice chat?

27
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:04,280
Let me tell you why I don't accept it.

28
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:05,120
It accepted it.

29
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,480
It didn't.

30
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,560
Thank you, judge.

31
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,200
Thank you, really.

32
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:11,200
I, Xiao Longnv, will remember this.

33
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,280
You really...

34
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,480
Stop playing with your phone.

35
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,760
In such a formal occasion,

36
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:17,680
stop playing with your phone, okay? Listen to me.

37
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,280
Okay. What do you want?

38
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:18,960
Come here and thank it. Come.

39
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,400
I won't. It's too hard.

40
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,680
You are so ignorant.

41
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,940
He's ignorant. Let's not argue with him.

42
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,480
Drive slowly.

43
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,520
It's been so long, you...

44
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,280
I can't forget this.

45
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,920
Xiaolong, actually, for this case,

46
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,050
if it were a different region or judge,

47
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,500
the verdict might have been very different.

48
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:58,680
I know.

49
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,720
You don't need to comfort me.

50
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,280
Winning and losing are common in battle.

51
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,540
I'm an adult, how could I not understand?

52
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:09,000
A loss is a loss. I accept it.

53
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,280
I will also urge Shengkang Insurance

54
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:17,339
to strengthen the standard training for their agents.

55
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,120
They must explain all the clauses

56
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:19,880
and restrictions

57
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:22,740
to the clients more carefully and professionally.

58
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:25,120
And the definition of diseases in the contract

59
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,980
should be further standardized.

60
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,400
That would be best,

61
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,400
to prevent inequality from the source.

62
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,000
Anyway,

63
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,080
you are a good opponent.

64
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,880
You too.

65
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,560
Why do I feel so nauseous?

66
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,600
Where is this?

67
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,800
Did we change venues?

68
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:58,000
Not bad, Xiao Longnv.

69
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:00,280
You even called a luxury car.

70
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,560
Luo Zhi, come give me a hand. Quick.

71
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,400
What's wrong, Director? Let me help.

72
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,120
Quick.

73
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:15,880
Lawyer Li.

74
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,840
How did Uncle get so drunk?

75
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:19,200
Doesn't he have some kind of antibody?

76
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,160
He has nothing. It's a total lie.

77
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,120
Oh my god.

78
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,120
Slow down. There are steps.

79
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,800
No need.

80
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:25,810
I'll walk by myself.

81
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,520
One, two, three.

82
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,680
Be careful.

83
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,360
Watch your back.

84
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,600
Thank you, Lawyer Li.

85
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,420
Come here quickly.

86
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,410
Have some tofu pudding to sober up.

87
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:11,240
I'm fine. It's all evaporated.

88
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,800
Evaporated?

89
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,720
Dad knows you drank.

90
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,320
You feel bad after drinking.

91
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:17,480
Xiaolong.

92
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,160
When will the cycle of revenge end?

93
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,480
What's the next line?

94
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,360
Only envy mandarin ducks, not immortals.

95
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,690
Stop talking nonsense.

96
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:26,080
Be forgiving when possible.

97
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,160
Really?

98
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,920
Why are you beating around the bush?

99
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,240
Just say it straight.

100
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:35,680
No, I...

101
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:37,610
Because I understand how you feel.

102
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:40,080
Because I've never lost a fight in the past.

103
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:41,800
No, no, no.

104
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,600
I lost once.

105
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,040
To Zhao Deqing, your Uncle Daqing.

106
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,159
You two fought?

107
00:06:47,159 --> 00:06:48,600
Weren't you on the same side?

108
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,240
We didn't know each other then.

109
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:50,920
We didn't.

110
00:06:51,159 --> 00:06:52,480
Once we got into a big fight.

111
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,409
After the fight,

112
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:54,159
we fought back and forth,

113
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:55,840
and became brothers.

114
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,040
Dad, what do you mean?

115
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,040
Do you mean

116
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,680
I should take Li Xin as my underling?

117
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,240
No, what underling?

118
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:04,920
I'm telling you the principle of turning enemies into friends.

119
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:07,160
If you two keep fighting like this,

120
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,360
when will it end?

121
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,160
But if you join forces with Xiaoxin,

122
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:10,720
then...

123
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,160
how many big cases will you solve in the future?

124
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:12,600
Right?

125
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,920
Does what I say make sense?

126
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,600
Yes, you see the big picture.

127
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,600
You see, when it comes to employing people,

128
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,130
your dad is very strategic.

129
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,920
It's called maneuvering and being far-sighted.

130
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:25,800
Dad, how do you write 'maneuvering'?

131
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,480
It's...

132
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,160
Why are you asking me this?

133
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,040
With your education, you should know this word.

134
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:33,800
Yes, my bad.

135
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,560
I'll look it up later.

136
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,159
Manager Xiao,

137
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,100
what time is it?

138
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,360
What time is it?

139
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,000
Slow down.

140
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,360
What happened again?

141
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:58,480
Did you pull a muscle?

142
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:00,480
I took a drunkard home last night.

143
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:03,280
Who? Xiao?

144
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:04,800
She's not heavy.

145
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,800
She's not heavy.

146
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,400
No, it wasn't her.

147
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,730
Help... help me lift it.

148
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,840
You should be more careful.

149
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,640
Make yourself comfortable.

150
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,860
After all these years, tell me the truth.

151
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,000
How did you really get this injury?

152
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:27,400
Bitten by a dog.

153
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,600
Do you think I really can't tell?

154
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,160
This is a sharp force injury.

155
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,720
Half a centimeter off, and it would have hit your spine.

156
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:34,450
You'd be in a wheelchair for the rest of your life.

157
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,880
Forget it if you don't want to talk about it.

158
00:08:39,159 --> 00:08:41,360
If there's anything you can't get over,

159
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:45,760
our hospital's psychological rehabilitation department is pretty good.

160
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,160
It's long gone.

161
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:35,800
Yesterday,

162
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,680
was I really brought back by that suitcase?

163
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,160
Would I lie to you?

164
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:42,720
Lawyer Li escorted you all the way to your bed.

165
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:46,120
Why don't I have any memory of it?

166
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:46,480
Uncle.

167
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,000
You were so drunk.

168
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,980
How could you remember anything?

169
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,360
My shoulder hurts so much.

170
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,740
Did he sneak-attack me while I was drunk?

171
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,720
What? What did you see?

172
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:04,840
I know, Uncle.

173
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:05,840
He hit me.

174
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,840
No, no, no.

175
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,240
Let's say you're Lawyer Li,

176
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,120
and I'm you.

177
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,720
Lawyer Li is tall.

178
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,840
He was holding you up, right?

179
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:12,480
You had your arm around him.

180
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,360
You were so heavy.

181
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,720
When you dropped your weight,

182
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,850
your shoulder hurt.

183
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:16,860
Get out of here.

184
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,370
Is he taller than me?

185
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,720
I'm 1.83 meters tall barefoot.

186
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,000
My legs alone are 1.2 meters long.

187
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,600
Does he have my proportions?

188
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,720
He must be this much taller than you.

189
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,120
He's only taller because he was wearing leather shoes.

190
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,120
I was wearing sneakers

191
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,050
with flat soles.

192
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:32,240
You haven't even joined the law firm yet.

193
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:34,480
Can you watch what you say?

194
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:35,840
Who is taller?

195
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:37,720
You are.

196
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,000
You are. You are.

197
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,930
Stop talking. Sister Long is here.

198
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,360
What is it?

199
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,120
Why are you looking at me?

200
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:58,520
Are your eyes glued to me?

201
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,040
It's nothing.

202
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,840
You... alright.

203
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:07,720
Anyway,

204
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,200
let's summarize our failed experience

205
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,120
and review it.

206
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,600
Luo Zhi, go get your summary report

207
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:15,600
and bring it to me.

208
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:19,720
From now on, you'll be responsible for our law firm's reception records

209
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,840
and case data collection.

210
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,240
What are you staring at? Get to work.

211
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:31,720
Okay, Lawyer Xiao.

212
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,480
This kid really needs to change his habit of making a fuss over nothing.

213
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,360
What's wrong?

214
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,840
Is my staircase okay?

215
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:48,720
Congratulations, Master,

216
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,360
on securing the long-term contract with Shengkang Insurance

217
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,360
and completing Department Two's

218
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,120
KPI for this year ahead of schedule.

219
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:54,000
The main thing is that we beat Xiao Longnv.

220
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,400
Wonderful.

221
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,440
It was all his idea.

222
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:58,720
Okay.

223
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,480
You clean this up later.

224
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:01,780
Have a seat.

225
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,840
Everyone has worked hard recently.

226
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,600
I'm treating everyone to dinner this Friday.

227
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:08,640
Ruoqi, help me book a restaurant.

228
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:10,000
Sure, leave it to me.

229
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,600
Okay.

230
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,840
Let's talk about the plan for this week.

231
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,240
The legal director of Star Alliance Airlines

232
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:15,720
sent me a link this morning.

233
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,000
He said a passenger

234
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,720
filmed a video on a flight

235
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,480
showing poor service by the crew.

236
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:22,360
It has already attracted some attention.

237
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:24,360
They are afraid that if the video continues to spread,

238
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,480
it will have a negative impact on the company's image.

239
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,600
They want us to send a letter to the platform to take down the video.

240
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,600
Okay, I'll leave this matter to you.

241
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:33,480
You two are just chatting here, huh?

242
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:35,240
The water just boiled. I was about to bring it to you.

243
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,080
I won't listen to your excuses.

244
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:36,840
I'll report this to the airline.

245
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,040
What kind of service attitude is this?

246
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,300
Sir, please calm down.

247
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,320
That was the situation at the time.

248
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,180
That passenger seemed to be sick.

249
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:44,680
He asked for hot water several times.

250
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,720
But the flight attendant didn't serve him.

251
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,680
Then they started arguing.

252
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,360
I have a fever of 40 degrees!

253
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,760
What kind of service is this?

254
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:49,480
We understand.

255
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:50,360
I'm going to file a complaint against her, you know?

256
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,520
Yes, I am the chief purser.

257
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,440
Please tell me if you have any issues.

258
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,840
You're the chief purser? I'll complain about you too!

259
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,600
What's your name?

260
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:55,240
Sir, please don't.

261
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:55,840
What's your name?

262
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:56,720
Don't do this.

263
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:59,120
You're not going to tell me, are you?

264
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,000
This is too much.

265
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:06,000
Jiayi, you must be terrified.

266
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:10,600
Miaomiao.

267
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,120
Can you do me a favor?

268
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,520
Don't you work at Honghu?

269
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,300
Can you introduce me to a good lawyer?

270
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:32,640
Actually, I've already resigned from Honghu.

271
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:35,370
But I haven't dared to tell my parents about this.

272
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:38,080
If they knew, they definitely wouldn't agree.

273
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,480
Then what are you doing now?

274
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,480
I'm now working independently

275
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:45,000
with a really good lawyer.

276
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,240
She used to be at Honghu too.

277
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,240
She's amazing.

278
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:49,600
How about I tell her about your situation?

279
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,840
She can definitely get justice for you.

280
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:57,720
Brother, just put your heart back in your chest,

281
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,480
okay?

282
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,840
The cases our law firm handles

283
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:00,720
are much more complicated than yours,

284
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,320
and we won them all in the end.

285
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:05,120
Okay.

286
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,720
Jiayi, this is our law firm.

287
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:07,520
Have a seat.

288
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,600
You're Miaomiao's classmate, right?

289
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:10,640
I'm Miaomiao's Brother Hu.

290
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:11,840
You can call me Brother Hu too.

291
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,480
Sit.

292
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:12,840
We're all friends here, sit.

293
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,240
You sit. I'll go get you some water.

294
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,000
Come, sit.

295
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,240
Sit.

296
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,840
Come, have some sunflower seeds.

297
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:20,600
These seeds are really good,

298
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,860
not stale at all. Come.

299
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,480
Hello, I'm Luo Zhi.

300
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:25,600
I'm also part of the team.

301
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,240
Right, if you have any problems, just say it.

302
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:27,900
Brother Hu,

303
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,000
go do your work.

304
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:31,140
Here, have some water, Jiayi.

305
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,640
Come, come over here.

306
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:39,180
How much commission do you get for bringing in a client?

307
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,360
Five hundred?

308
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,840
I'll slap you.

309
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:44,240
This is my classmate. I'm helping her out.

310
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:46,480
You look like an idiot. Get out.

311
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:47,620
Step aside.

312
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:48,480
You,

313
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,840
you go with your uncle.

314
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:57,000
It's okay.

315
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:01,170
What are you looking at?

316
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,850
The client's look isn't right.

317
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,050
What do you mean?

318
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,360
She probably thinks you're a hooligan.

319
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,120
What? I'm a very civilized person.

320
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,120
I'm a hooligan?

321
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:13,180
Uncle, you call yourself civilized?

322
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,840
Good morning, Director.

323
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:17,240
You startled me with your sudden outburst.

324
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,240
Look at how sunny and positive he is,

325
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:22,400
unlike you, looking gloomy all day.

326
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:25,280
Very good. Keep it up.

327
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,480
After you, Director.

328
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,840
When it comes to kissing up,

329
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,240
you're the master.

330
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:32,840
It's not kissing up.

331
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:35,600
Leaders in big law firms are all called directors.

332
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:37,360
Which Popeye is called a director?

333
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,720
Big law firm.

334
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,980
Big law firm. Go get your tongue checked.

335
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:51,000
Jiayi, I've already watched the video.

336
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:54,000
Could you tell me more about what happened then?

337
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,480
While the plane was descending,

338
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,000
he asked me for hot water.

339
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,120
Ladies and gentlemen,

340
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,520
the plane is descending.

341
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,640
Please return to your seats

342
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,170
and fasten your seatbelts.

343
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:16,840
Hello, Mr. Hu.

344
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:18,000
How can I help you?

345
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:21,000
Bring me a cup of hot water and a hot towel.

346
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:22,320
I'm sorry, Mr. Hu.

347
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,400
Our plane is currently descending.

348
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,000
Our food carts have been sealed.

349
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
I'll bring it to you as soon as we land.

350
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:28,840
I can't wait.

351
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:30,360
I have a bad cold right now.

352
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:33,000
I just want some hot water, okay?

353
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:36,520
Okay, I'll go ask the chief purser.

354
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,360
What's wrong with you guys?

355
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:39,600
You were already delayed.

356
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,640
And now it's so hard just to get some water.

357
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,600
Hurry up.

358
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,000
Sorry for the trouble.

359
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:48,000
Chief purser, a passenger wants hot water.

360
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,160
For safety reasons,

361
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:52,220
give him a bottle of room-temperature water first.

362
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,480
Mr. Hu, your water.

363
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:56,600
What is this?

364
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:57,840
No, I want hot water.

365
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,480
Why did you bring me cold water?

366
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,720
Can't you understand human speech?

367
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,840
I have a fever right now.

368
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:02,840
My whole body is shivering.

369
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:03,840
And you give me cold water.

370
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,480
What? Are you trying to kill me?

371
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,720
Mr. Hu, please let me explain.

372
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,599
Explain what? What kind of service is this?

373
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:09,960
I want hot water.

374
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,119
Go get me hot water right now.

375
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:12,839
I'm sorry, Mr. Hu.

376
00:17:12,839 --> 00:17:14,000
Please don't be angry.

377
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,400
I'll go resolve the hot water issue for you.

378
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:20,599
Chief Purser, that passenger insists on hot water.

379
00:17:20,599 --> 00:17:21,839
He says room temperature is too cold.

380
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:23,640
But the plane is about to land.

381
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:25,599
But he looks really uncomfortable.

382
00:17:25,599 --> 00:17:28,119
Can we make an exception and give it to him?

383
00:17:28,119 --> 00:17:28,600
How about this.

384
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:29,600
You go boil it first,

385
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,360
and bring it to him after we land.

386
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:31,880
Okay.

387
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:38,400
Ladies and gentlemen,

388
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:41,760
our flight has safely arrived at its destination.

389
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,840
Chief Purser, my work is done.

390
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:46,480
I'll go bring it to that passenger.

391
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,840
I've been waiting there for hot water,

392
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,120
and you two are just chatting here, huh?

393
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,240
Sir, the water just boiled.

394
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:50,720
I was just about to bring it to you.

395
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:51,520
What do you mean just about to?

396
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:52,520
What kind of service attitude is that?

397
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:53,240
Sir, sir.

398
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,120
What's your name? Please calm down.

399
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:54,480
Please take a seat first.

400
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,360
I'm not going back to my seat.

401
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,600
When the plane was in the air,

402
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:57,360
I asked you to get water.

403
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:58,480
Now we've landed.

404
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,720
I have a fever of 40 degrees.

405
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,840
I'm burning up! What are you doing?

406
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:01,600
Sir, I'm the Chief Purser.

407
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,240
Talk to me if you have an issue. Why should I talk to you?

408
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,360
I'll complain about you too.

409
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,320
What's your name?

410
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:07,000
I don't want you. I want to complain about her.

411
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,120
Let me see. You have a name tag, right?

412
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:08,920
Let me see what your name is.

413
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:09,680
Sir, what kind of behavior is this?

414
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:11,200
I'm just looking at the tag, what behavior?

415
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:11,800
Let me see.

416
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:23,480
I heard you called the police later, right?

417
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:25,000
Yes.

418
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,000
But the police said

419
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:31,320
it didn't reach the level of criminal molestation,

420
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,460
so they didn't file a case.

421
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:36,760
So do you want to sue him

422
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,480
for molestation now?

423
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,940
Actually, I respect the police's decision.

424
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,000
It's just that

425
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,480
psychologically,

426
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,480
I'm having some problems right now.

427
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:53,000
I failed the airline's regular assessment,

428
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,480
so I can't fly now.

429
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:57,570
The doctor also told me to rest for a while.

430
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,480
But whenever I think of that scene,

431
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,000
I don't understand what I did wrong.

432
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,480
Lawyer Xiao.

433
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:16,280
I want to seek justice for myself.

434
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,640
I want him to apologize to me.

435
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:23,640
Sister Long, Jiayi used to be very cheerful.

436
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:27,040
I've never seen her in this state before.

437
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:28,480
She's gone.

438
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:29,640
What kind of case is it?

439
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:31,370
I think this girl is a bit weird.

440
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,720
Watch your mouth.

441
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:34,200
What do you mean weird?

442
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,480
You're the weird one.

443
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:38,000
No, I mean her mental state seems very poor.

444
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,160
She's sick.

445
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:41,000
She has ASD.

446
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,760
Getting this disease at such a young age?

447
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,000
What is ASD?

448
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,400
ASD is Acute Stress Disorder.

449
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:46,880
Excuse me.

450
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:48,320
It refers to a transient mental disorder

451
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,480
that occurs within minutes or hours

452
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,320
after experiencing an acute

453
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:54,280
and severe psychological trauma.

454
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:55,400
ASD (Acute Stress Disorder)

455
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,720
is also a clearly defined mental disorder

456
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,480
in the International Classification of Diseases.

457
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:00,240
There will be symptoms like hyperarousal, avoidance,

458
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,480
and re-experiencing the trauma.

459
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:09,280
Her psychological evaluation report says so.

460
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:11,440
She will suffer from insomnia, headaches,

461
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:13,760
loss of appetite, and tachycardia,

462
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:18,240
and she will feel uncomfortable around the opposite sex.

463
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:21,240
Right. Just now, when my uncle got close to her,

464
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:21,920
she was scared.

465
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:23,000
Get out of here.

466
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,240
Aren't you of the opposite sex?

467
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,000
I... I look kind.

468
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,200
Sister Long, we must help Jiayi

469
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,280
and get justice for her.

470
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:29,480
How can we get justice?

471
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,680
The police said

472
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,000
they couldn't file a case.

473
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,200
Not filing a case means

474
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,720
it's not that serious. How can you get justice?

475
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:36,440
We can.

476
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:39,240
According to the Civil Code of the People's Republic of China,

477
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,480
Article 118...

478
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,000
Enough. It's not your turn to speak.

479
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,320
Gu Miaomiao, I have to criticize you.

480
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:45,760
What kind of cases are you bringing in?

481
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:46,720
Don't bring them in anymore.

482
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:49,380
Leave professional matters to professionals.

483
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:52,640
Look, if it were a physical injury,

484
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:54,000
we would examine the injury

485
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
and grade it accordingly.

486
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,640
But,

487
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,680
how do we calculate her psychological trauma?

488
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:59,440
What? Isn't psychological trauma a trauma?

489
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,160
Exactly.

490
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:02,720
Psychological trauma is just like physical trauma.

491
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:03,480
They are both traumas.

492
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:05,480
Well, I've been wronged a lot since I was a kid.

493
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,480
I don't see myself having this or that trauma.

494
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:09,000
I was only ever injured by a bicycle.

495
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,600
This case is just hard to win.

496
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:12,720
Look at these fine little cases in my hands.

497
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:14,480
Is it up to you to decide if they are easy to fight?

498
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,480
Why don't you go fight them?

499
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,920
Aren't I the one fighting?

500
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,000
Are you afraid I'll lose,

501
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:18,840
or are you afraid for yourself?

502
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:21,000
Okay, okay, okay. What are you thinking?

503
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,330
Am I that kind of person?

504
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,680
Then let's fight. Fight, fight, fight.

505
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:35,000
Oh my God.

506
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,000
I once said

507
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,940
that you can't be a good person in this world.

508
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:41,680
No good deed goes unpunished.

509
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,480
Regarding the flight attendant,

510
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:44,520
the police were on my side at the time.

511
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:46,320
Isn't everyone on the internet scolding the airline too?

512
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,480
Look at this lousy flight attendant.

513
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,160
I didn't sue her,

514
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,240
but she turned around and sued me.

515
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:50,640
Do you think she's crazy?

516
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:52,440
Mr. Hu,

517
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:55,080
your purpose for calling me here today is to sue her.

518
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,720
Absolutely. We must sue her.

519
00:21:56,760 --> 00:21:58,480
Also, the airline that flight attendant works for

520
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:00,280
is doing nothing.

521
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:01,320
They are aiding and abetting.

522
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,320
I'll file a complaint against them.

523
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:03,980
I'll deal with them together.

524
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:06,480
Well,

525
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,480
let me propose a toast.

526
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:09,240
Thank you, boss, for treating us to barbecue today.

527
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,240
Thank you, boss.

528
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:11,400
Thank you, boss.

529
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:13,930
I'll drink to that. Thanks for your hard work.

530
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:17,610
I can tell Ruoqi has a good tolerance for alcohol.

531
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:21,720
Lawyer Li, why do you never drink?

532
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,000
Drinking affects judgment.

533
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:23,880
Let me cut it.

534
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,000
Affects judgment.

535
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,080
I'm really curious about what kind of personality Lawyer Li has.

536
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:30,160
Does not drinking affect personality too?

537
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,800
I'm talking about the recently popular

538
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:33,320
16 personalities test.

539
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:35,400
Lawyer Li must be

540
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,440
an introvert.

541
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:43,580
Absolutely rational.

542
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:45,520
Boss, let's have a drink.

543
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,480
What took you so long on the phone?

544
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:49,320
It was a call from the airline.

545
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,000
They said Xu Jiayi

546
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,560
has officially sued Hu Sheng.

547
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:54,160
Hu Sheng's side is furious.

548
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,440
Now they are making a scene at the airline.

549
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:56,760
The airline doesn't want to blow things out of proportion.

550
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:58,040
They want to act as a mediator

551
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,080
to facilitate a settlement between the two parties

552
00:22:59,080 --> 00:23:00,520
and get Xu Jiayi to drop the lawsuit.

553
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:01,920
It wasn't a big deal originally,

554
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:04,240
but now it's become very troublesome.

555
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:06,240
Is it as troublesome as my construction dispute?

556
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:08,640
Is it as troublesome as my medical dispute?

557
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,640
You two are so stupid.

558
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,400
I'm in more trouble than both of you.

559
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:15,160
The lawyer Xu Jiayi hired is Xiao Longnü.

560
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,760
